# suite-declarations.manifest — every tracked test suite that does NOT declare
# a population to the `guards-for-diff` index, with its status. Recorded as
# DATA so that non-declaration is an EXPLICIT, ENUMERATED, REVIEWABLE property
# instead of the silent default (your-org/nexus-code#1301 item 3, #1078).
#
# Enforced by:  bash monitor/watcher/test-suite-declaration-census.sh
#
# ── WHY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `guards-for-diff` prints "N of M tracked test suites do not declare a
# population and are INVISIBLE to this index". Invisible is not excluded: a
# non-declaring suite appears in neither SELECTED nor CONSIDERED-AND-EXCLUDED,
# so its absence reads as a considered exclusion (#1078), and on 2026-09-05 the
# ONE guard with something to say about a change (test-guard-closure-boundary)
# was among the invisible while 52 selected guards all passed (#1301). The
# question item 3 asks is whether a suite MAY be enrolled in nothing at all.
# This file answers: yes, but only by SAYING SO, per suite, with a reason —
# and a NEW suite must either declare a population or be classified here,
# never land silently in the blind spot.
#
# ── STATUS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   declares-none  reviewed: the suite reads no repo-wide population (a unit
#                  test over its own fixtures); enrolling it would declare an
#                  empty set. The reason says what it reads instead.
#   unreviewed     nobody has yet asked; the census default. Bounded by the
#                  ceiling below — a ratchet that only goes down as suites are
#                  reviewed (moved to declares-none, or taught gp_population
#                  and REMOVED from this file).
#
# The generator is the index's own predicate (both tokens: `gp_handle "$@"`
# and `gp_population()`), so this file and guards-for-diff cannot disagree
# about who declares.
#
# unreviewed-ceiling: 370
#
# ── ROWS  suite|status|reason ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
